----------------------------------------------------------\n### 5.  Verification that the family covers \\(T_n\\)\n\nTake any \\((a,b)\\in T_n\\).\n\n*If \\(a\\le k\\)*, the vertical line \\(V_a:x=a\\) (present) contains the point.\n\n*If \\(a>k\\)*, then from \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) we obtain \\(b\\le n+1-a < n+1-k\\), i.e.\n\\(b\\le n-k\\). The horizontal line \\(H_b:y=b\\) (still present) contains the\npoint.\n\nThus every required lattice point lies on at least one of the \\(n\\) constructed\nlines.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 6.  Conclusion\n\nFor each integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) we have exhibited a set of \\(n\\)\ndistinct lines, exactly \\(k\\) of which are sunny, that covers all points of\n\\(T_n\\).  No further restriction on \\(k\\) is needed.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{All integers }k\\text{ with }0\\le k\\le n\\text{ are possible.}}\n\\]"
